CLANPROGRESSION CLANPROGRESS CLANFAVOR CLANINSPECT

CLAN PROGRESSION READOUTS

  clan progress [clan-incarnation-uid]
  clan favor [after-incarnation-uid]

Clan progress shows your current SQL clan, Clan XP/level, shared Influence,
your cumulative Favor and standing, account contribution usage and UTC weekly
reset, the last committed personal award and any reductions, and buff unlocks,
active slots and family cooldowns. Readouts do not award or spend anything.
They report when progression earning or buff activation is disabled.

Your authenticated account ID determines contribution limits. Alts and clan
changes share the same account allowance. Missing account identity or storage
is reported as unavailable, rather than granting a fresh allowance.

Clan favor lists your saved Favor history, including former and disbanded
clans, with each incarnation's immutable UID. Use clan progress <uid> to view
your own retained standing. Current accepted members can see shared balances;
applicants and former members cannot inspect those balances. A new clan that
reuses an old clan number does not inherit its Favor, XP, Influence or timers.
If there are more history entries, the output gives the command for the next
page. History does not grant access to a former clan's services.

Amounts retain exact eighth-point fractions. Favor is cumulative and is not
spent on purchases. Legacy clan points and bank deposits are separate from
Favor and Clan XP. The existing clan award command does not award Favor.

Buff tiers share one cooldown per incarnation and family. Cancellation and
expiry release the slot but do not shorten the saved next-use time. Changing
tier, slot, officer or membership cannot reset it. These readouts do not
activate, cancel, refresh or replace a buff.

STAFF INSPECTION
  clan inspect <character-id> <account-id> <clan-incarnation-uid>

Greater staff may inspect retained clan/character progression and the explicitly
selected account's usage. The character and account IDs are separate inspection
keys; this command does not assert that they belong together. Clan rank or
officer permissions do not grant access to this staff tool. It cannot mint or
edit any earned currency, counter, receipt or cooldown.
See also: CLANBUFFS, CLAN
